/-!
# Deductions for the long-root exclusion

The action leaf constructs the normalizer intersection acting on `C_T(X)`,
identifies its faithful action quotient, and proves the TI, invariant-intersection
and orbit-index deductions. The seven-action leaf eliminates the order-21
image once the two intrinsic automorphism-image bounds in the covered `G₂(4)`
case have been established. It uses `O^{7′}(M)`, not `O₇(M)`. The O'Nan leaf
connects linear subspaces with the actual subgroup action and eliminates all
four alternatives once the geometry and intrinsic bounds are supplied.

These are conditional deductions for Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript
(1 March 2004), Lemma 16.5.13, printed pp.1201--1202. The root-parabolic
construction, its identification with the common residual, the O'Nan input,
and the intrinsic covered-module bounds are still needed. No source-numbered
long-root exclusion is asserted before these premises are discharged.
-/
